menu "Brake_light configuration"

    config CHMBL_CLI
        bool "Enable developer CLI (console shell)"
        default y
        help
            Build the developer command-line shell (design element DE-00). It
            runs over the console transport selected per target in
            sdkconfig.defaults.<target> (USB Serial/JTAG on the ESP32-C3, UART
            on the classic ESP32).

            Disable for production builds; the shell is then absent from the
            image.

    comment "Brake bar (DE-04) — binary output, no brightness/PWM"

    config CHMBL_BAR_EN_A_GPIO
        int "Brake-bar string A driver enable GPIO (U3 CTRL)"
        range -1 33
        default 5 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3
        default 2 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
        default 2
        help
            GPIO (IOxx) driving the enable/CTRL pin of the first AP3019A boost
            LED driver on the brake_light PCB. Active high: high = that string
            lit at the current setpoint fixed by its 560 mohm sense resistor,
            low = dark. This is a STATIC enable, not a PWM dimming input —
            brightness/dimming is deferred, see
            docs/design/de-04-led-render.md.

            PROVISIONAL on the ESP32-C3. U3's CTRL pad is NOT wired to the MCU
            in the committed first-pass schematic/PCB (it reads as
            "unconnected-(U3-CTRL-Pad4)" in the board netlist), so this
            default is a firmware-side proposal pending a schematic review, not
            a verified assignment. See brake_light/hardware/README.md for the
            pin map and what was verified from the netlist.

            Classic ESP32 (bench dev board) default GPIO2 = the onboard LED, so
            the bar's on/off behaviour is observable on a DevKitC. On a
            C3-DevKitM bench board set this to 8 for the same reason.

            -1 = string not fitted (skip the pin entirely).

    config CHMBL_BAR_EN_B_GPIO
        int "Brake-bar string B driver enable GPIO (U6 CTRL)"
        range -1 33
        default 6 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3
        default -1 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
        default -1
        help
            Same as CHMBL_BAR_EN_A_GPIO for the second AP3019A driver. The
            ~8" bar is split into two series strings (10 emitters each on the
            first-pass PCB); the firmware drives both enables together as one
            logical output, so the bar never lights half-on.

            PROVISIONAL on the ESP32-C3 for the same reason as string A: U6's
            CTRL pad is unconnected in the committed board netlist.

            Defaults to -1 (not fitted) on the classic ESP32 bench board,
            which has only one stand-in LED.

    config CHMBL_RENDER_TICK_MS
        int "Render task period (ms)"
        range 5 100
        default 16
        help
            How often the render stage re-evaluates the effective state and
            re-drives the bar (~60 Hz by default, per docs/firmware.md §2).
            Also the granularity at which a change deferred by the anti-strobe
            floor gets committed.

    config CHMBL_RENDER_MIN_ON_MS
        int "Anti-strobe: minimum bar ON time (ms)"
        range 0 5000
        default 600
        help
            Once the bar is lit it stays lit at least this long (BL-RND-2).
            This is the floor that actually prevents a strobe, and it is safe
            to make generous: holding a brake light on slightly too long is
            honest, flashing it is both a safety and a regulatory problem
            (docs/safety-regulatory.md §1).

    config CHMBL_RENDER_MIN_OFF_MS
        int "Anti-strobe: minimum bar OFF time (ms)"
        range 0 2000
        default 150
        help
            Once the bar is dark it stays dark at least this long before it may
            relight. Kept small: this is the only floor that can delay a
            brake-ON edge against the <= 100 ms end-to-end budget
            (ARCHITECTURE.md §5), and it only bites if the bar went dark
            moments ago.

    comment "Status indicator (DE-10 slice) — separate from the bar"

    config CHMBL_STATUS_LED_GRN_GPIO
        int "Status LED GRN (D14) GPIO"
        range -1 33
        default 10 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3
        default 5 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the green status LED D14 through R20 (100 ohm).
            Active high (anode-fed, cathode on GND — this orientation IS
            verified from the board netlist).

            PROVISIONAL pin number on the ESP32-C3: R20's upper pad is
            unconnected in the committed board netlist
            ("unconnected-(R20-Pad1)"), so which GPIO drives it is not yet
            decided in hardware.

            -1 = not fitted.

    config CHMBL_STATUS_LED_RED_GPIO
        int "Status LED RED (D13) GPIO"
        range -1 33
        default 7 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3
        default 4 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the red status LED D13 through R21 (100 ohm). Active
            high. PROVISIONAL pin number for the same reason as the green LED
            ("unconnected-(R21-Pad1)").

            -1 = not fitted.

    config CHMBL_STATUS_BLINK_MS
        int "Status LED blink half-period (ms)"
        range 150 2000
        default 500
        help
            Half-period of the status indicator's slow blink (link WAITING =
            green blink, link LOST = red blink). Floored well above a strobe
            rate (BL-IND-4). This paces the *status LED only* — the brake bar
            is never blinked.

    comment "ESP-NOW link (DE-01 / DE-03)"

    config CHMBL_NET_CHANNEL
        int "ESP-NOW Wi-Fi channel"
        range 1 13
        default 6
        help
            Fixed 2.4 GHz channel used for ESP-NOW. Must match the
            transmitter's CHMBL_NET_CHANNEL — there's no channel-agreement
            handshake yet (see docs/design/de-01-espnow-link.md open items).

    config CHMBL_PAIR_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Pairing window (seconds)"
        range 3 60
        default 15
        help
            How long `pair start` broadcasts/listens for a peer before
            giving up.

    config CHMBL_LINK_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Link-loss timeout (ms)"
        range 50 2000
        default 300
        help
            No valid heartbeat for longer than this and the link watchdog
            (DE-03) declares the link lost. Protocol target is <= 300 ms
            (docs/protocol.md §4).

    config CHMBL_LINK_TICK_MS
        int "Link watchdog tick (ms)"
        range 20 500
        default 100
        help
            How often the link watchdog re-evaluates link health and
            republishes the effective braking state to the render stage and
            the link status to the indicator (~10 Hz by default, per
            docs/firmware.md §2).

endmenu
